  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="2272-d513-7c11-1251" name="Etruscan (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #2 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). 700 BC to 280 BC The Etruscan people dominated the North of Italy for several centuries, gradually expanding to control the Po valley and the coastal areas of central Italy. They were circumscribed by the Alps and, later, Celt migrations to the North and by the Greek colonies to the South, and never controlled the central mountain region. They were eventually overcome by the Latin League and in later times, utilised the Roman military system and equipment. The list is intended to represent their army in its distinctive period around 500 BC. Allies And Mercenaries: The Etruscans allied with most of the other powers of Italy and may take allies from the Italian Hill Tribes or Gallic lists, and may take allies from both at the same time.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Etruscan]
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Characters: up to 25% Cavalry: up to 25% Infantry: At least 50% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 50%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
